//RS /// Every source file this package compiles, sorted, without `scan`'s parse
//RS /// pass: the same authority-checked enumeration the part index is built from,
//RS /// minus package manifests and nested packages. Tooling that must act on every
//RS /// file in the package — bare `jet test` collecting `#Test` blocks package-wide
//RS /// (spec S43) — enumerates here instead of walking the filesystem again, so the
//RS /// file set stays the project scan's, not a second opinion about it. An
//RS /// authority failure yields an empty set: the caller's ordinary compile path
//RS /// reports the real error rather than a second, worse copy of it.
